Thea is a browser-based binary visualization explorer.

Start with [docs/README.md](docs/README.md) for running the app, current architecture,
factor recipes, rendering internals, tests, and planned direction.

Original design sketch (broader than the currently implemented Blob-based viewer):

thea is a data visualization platform

it is built from a few simple core concepts:

sources, incoming streams of data
buffers, holds incoming data streams up to a certain (potentially system limited) size, can be themselves streamed from
maps, translation layers that consume some kind of data stream and produce another
views, terminal points in the architecture that consume streams and render them to the display

the simplest data source variety is that of the byte stream, incoming data received as a sequence of 8-bit chunks
these chunks may be mapped into other sizes of data or perhaps have some structure imposed over them e.g. ascii-encoded gene data may be mapped to sequences of 2-bit objects
that may then further be mapped into 6-bit object sequences for codons

